# Project Atlas (EAGLES) — Cursor Rules

You are assisting a 2-founder team (Data Scientists, ~6 months of software
experience) building an enterprise work-management platform. Full context
lives in `docs/`. Read `CLAUDE.md` at the repo root for the canonical rule
set — this file mirrors it for Cursor.

## Before writing code

- Check `docs/02_Modules/<feature>.md` for the feature's Overview, Business
  Rules, Database, API, UI, Acceptance Criteria, Validation, and Future
  Scope. If it doesn't exist, stop and ask for it to be written first —
  documentation precedes implementation on this project.
- Check `docs/03_Database/` and `prisma/schema.prisma` for the actual
  schema. Never invent a table, column, or relation that isn't documented
  there.
- Check `docs/04_API/openapi.yaml` for the actual API contract. Never
  invent an endpoint or response shape.

## Architecture rules (enforced, not optional)

- Feature-first folders only:
  `src/features/<feature>/{components,hooks,services,repositories,validation,types,api}`.
- Prisma is imported ONLY inside `*.repository.ts` files.
- Route Handlers (`src/app/api/**/route.ts`) are thin: resolve session,
  delegate to a feature's service, map errors to HTTP responses. No
  business logic, no Prisma calls in `app/`.
- Services own business rules and RBAC checks. Every mutating service
  method takes an authenticated `actor` and authorizes before acting.
- Cross-feature calls go through another feature's service, never its
  repository or Prisma models.
- Every Prisma model has `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `createdBy`,
  `updatedBy`, `deletedAt`. No hard deletes from app code.

## Code style rules

- TypeScript `strict: true`. Never use `any`; use `unknown` + narrowing or
  a precise type instead.
- All external input validated with Zod before use; reuse the same schema
  for client (`zodResolver`) and server validation.
- No comments that restate the code. Comments only for non-obvious "why."
- Follow `docs/01_Architecture/04_Coding_Standards.md` for naming, error
  handling, and testing expectations.

## Portability rules

- Never call a Vercel-only API or a Supabase client SDK feature beyond
  Postgres connection + Storage from feature code. Storage goes through
  `shared/lib/storage/StorageAdapter`. See ADR-0004.

## When unsure

If a request would require guessing at a schema shape, an API contract, or
a business rule not yet documented, do not invent one — surface the gap
and propose a doc update instead of silently generating placeholder logic.
